karton (@VERSION@) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The guest's picture shows on an NVIDIA card under a native Wayland
    session (patch stereo3d/0004). Before, the GL scanout was imported as an
    EGL image from its stride alone, without the buffer's modifier or planes,
    so a driver that tiles its buffers read it as linear. Karton now builds
    the image the way spice-gtk's own EGL path does, with every plane, its
    offset and the buffer's modifier, drains stale GL errors before the bind,
    and says once when a scanout cannot be imported. The xcb platform keeps
    Qt's own integration choice (GLX by default): a compositor read-back
    showed that forcing EGL there leaves every Karton window black on NVIDIA
    under Xwayland, so that default waits for a measurement on real Xorg and
    on Mesa. ORDER 255.
  * Patches 0005 and 0006: when the picture cannot be imported the viewer
    says so, in place of the black window: that the picture cannot be shown,
    why in plain words, and what to do (the Wayland session, or
    QT_XCB_GL_INTEGRATION=xcb_egl where Qt's GLX integration gives no EGL
    display). The notice goes away when an import succeeds. The log line is
    written once for each distinct width, height, format and modifier, not
    for every scanout record. The three strings come in Polish, Brazilian
    Portuguese, French, German, Japanese, Korean and Simplified and
    Traditional Chinese, a first draft written with AI assistance, pending
    native speakers (a second model reviewed it and its corrections are
    applied). ORDER 255j.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  @DATE@
